    "name_suffix": "_2026",
    "teacher_markdown": "## Choice D — Teaching Tips (Card Styling Challenge)\r\n\r\n- **Encourage focused refinement.**  \r\n  Have students improve one card element at a time (spacing, shadows, image fit) and preview before layering additional changes.\r\n\r\n- **Push for clear goals before prompting.**  \r\n  If students ask for “better cards,” require them to name what feels off (crowded spacing, uneven images, inconsistent shadows).\r\n\r\n- **Watch for style changes that reduce usability.**  \r\n  Larger shadows, dramatic hover effects, or decorative borders should not reduce readability or make buttons harder to see. Encourage students to briefly resize the preview to confirm the cards still display clearly on smaller screens.\r\n\r\n- **Require clear version comments.**  \r\n  Students should state what they changed and why it improves clarity, consistency, or usability before saving.",
